jsonb_toaster_lite — TOAST/storage layer for jsonb
====================================================

Purpose
-------
jsonb_toaster_lite is a TOAST/storage layer for the standard
PostgreSQL jsonb type.  It uses the Pluggable TOAST API (contrib/toastapi)
to plug in custom physical storage strategies — sliced detoast,
compressed chunks, partial rewrite — while leaving jsonb's encoder
and decoder untouched in core.

Source provenance
-----------------
TOAST internals (chunk machinery, pointer constructors, sliced
detoast iterator, diff applier) are ported from
postgrespro/postgres@jsonb_toaster (contrib/jsonb_toaster) under
this extension's own jbtl_* / Jbtl* / JBTL_* symbol namespace.
Original symbol names from the postgrespro branch are referenced
only in port-trace comments where useful.

GSON discipline
---------------
This extension is GSON-free by construction.  No symbols from the
postgrespro generic-jsonb dispatch family are introduced here.  All
jsonb construction, traversal, and equality is handled by the
standard core API (utils/jsonb.h).  K1's KVMap (value-size sorting)
is a core feature and not duplicated here.

Status
------
L0.1 (this commit): handler skeleton.  tsr_validate accepts
jsonb columns with EXTENDED storage.  All other callbacks raise
"not yet implemented".  No storage logic.

Future commits will incrementally add (in order):
  L1.x   pointer types, custom-varlena constructors,
         chunk writer, chunk reader, sliced detoast
  L2     minimal storage round-trip
  L3     compressed chunks + sliced detoast benchmarking
